<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brinno</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brinno was a chieftain of the Cananefates, a Germanic people of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> delta. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a>, in 69 CE his people raised him on a shield to proclaim him leader, the earliest record of that custom, and he opened the Batavian revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-civilis">Julius Civilis</a> by attacking Roman forts on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> coast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brinno.jpg" alt="Brinno" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Barend Wijnveld · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SA_4999-Anno_70._Brinio_als_leider_der_Kaninefaten_op_het_schild_geheven.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
